            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous treatment of coronary bifurcation lesions in the era of drug-eluting stents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>577-89</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The current report provides an overview of the evolving techniques for percutaneous treatment of bifurcation lesions, including the approaches most commonly used in the current era of DES, and reviews the angiographic and clinical outcomes from clinical series published to date.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
